  "prompt": "Postgres: LISTEN, NOTIFY, UNLISTEN, DEALLOCATE and DISCARD are parsed as aliased columns\n\nPostgres' `LISTEN`, `UNLISTEN`, `NOTIFY`, `DEALLOCATE` and `DISCARD` statements are parsed as a column with an alias. Some come back as invalid SQL, and others don't parse at all.\n\n```python\nfrom sqlglot import transpile\nfor sql in [\"LISTEN c\", \"NOTIFY c\", \"DEALLOCATE p\", \"DISCARD ALL\"]:\n    print(transpile(sql, read=\"postgres\", write=\"postgres\"))\n# ['LISTEN AS c']\n# ['NOTIFY AS c']\n# ['DEALLOCATE AS p']\n# ['DISCARD AS ALL']\n\ntranspile(\"UNLISTEN *\", read=\"postgres\")             # ParseError: Required keyword: 'expression' missing\ntranspile(\"NOTIFY c, 'hi'\", read=\"postgres\")         # ParseError: Invalid expression / Unexpected token\ntranspile(\"DEALLOCATE PREPARE p\", read=\"postgres\")   # ParseError: Invalid expression / Unexpected token\n```\n\nPostgres 17 runs all of the original statements. Each rewritten one fails with `syntax error at or near \"AS\"`.\n\nThe Postgres tokenizer already maps similar statements (`DECLARE`, `DO`, `REINDEX`, `RESET`) to `TokenType.COMMAND`. Presto does the same for `DEALLOCATE PREPARE` (#4423).\n\nDocs: https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-listen.html, https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-notify.html, https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-unlisten.html, https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-deallocate.html, https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-discard.html",
